{"id": "EUVD-2014-9824", "enisaUuid": "730cb263-7913-3cf8-8eee-7ea7fbcc5c5a", "description": "DedeCMS 5.6 and 5.7 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to inject script by supplying unsanitized input to the adminDirHand parameter. Attackers can send crafted GET requests to /include/dialog/config.php that close the generated script tag and inject JavaScript, which executes in the victim's browser. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-23.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:52:20", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.cnblogs.com/milantgh/p/3615853.html", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/dedecms/dedecms-config-xss.yaml", "https://www.dedecms.com/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dedecms-5.6-5.7-reflected-xss-via-admindirhand-in-config-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2014-125131", "GHSA-4xjp-4vfj-2c62"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3c8cc0f0-afa0-3368-9f16-c532dea03fb7", "product": {"name": "DeDeCMS", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "5e00475e-b627-32bd-86bd-ab80e3a9079f", "product": {"name": "DeDeCMS", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6919ccf8-643f-3d95-84ac-cd708cd70a8e", "vendor": {"name": "DedeCMS"}}], "isExploited": false}